hls: a media playlist needed again starts afresh

A playlist that stops being needed keeps what it held then. Discarded
at the open (its streams discarded before the first read), it is closed
there, but its subdemuxer and I/O buffer keep the open's probe (part of
its first segment) and a buffered packet. Discarded later (after
avformat_find_stream_info(), as a player that picks its tracks after the
open does), it is read on until it needs a new segment, and dropped
there with that segment's early open (http_multiple) still pending.

Needed again, it read on from those. Stale packets from the start of the
stream came first (an audio rendition's at 0 s, after which the
catch-up ended), the subdemuxer ran them into the new segment's bytes
(corrupt packets; an fMP4 variant gave no packet at all, mov taking the
new fragments for parts of the old one); or the pending connection was
read in place of the segment due, and the segments after it were never
asked for (6 s segments: the new video or audio came 9 s late).

Drop them as a seek does: close the inputs, empty the buffer, flush the
subdemuxer, unref the packet and serve the init section again. Subtitle
playlists are reopened already.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -3478,6 +3478,25 @@ static int recheck_discard_flags(AVFormatContext *s, int first)
                 avformat_close_input(&pls->ctx);
                 free_subtitle_cues(pls);
             }
+            if (!pls->is_subtitle) {
+                /* A media playlist that stopped being read still holds what
+                 * its subdemuxer and I/O buffer had then (the open's probe,
+                 * part of a segment), and a packet: drop them, as a seek
+                 * does, or they come first, from where it stopped, and run
+                 * into the new segment's data (corrupt packets). */
+                AVIOContext *const pb = &pls->pb.pub;
+                ff_format_io_close(pls->parent, &pls->input);
+                pls->input_read_done = 0;
+                ff_format_io_close(pls->parent, &pls->input_next);
+                pls->input_next_requested = 0;
+                pls->input_next_error = 0;
+                av_packet_unref(pls->pkt);
+                pb->buf_end = pb->buf_ptr = pb->buffer;
+                pb->pos = 0;
+                if (pls->ctx)
+                    ff_read_frame_flush(pls->ctx);
+                pls->cur_init_section = NULL;
+            }
             pls->cur_seq_no = select_cur_seq_no(c, pls);
             pls->first_read_seq_no = -1;
             pls->reload_error_time = 0;
